# Checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Git's autocrlf default on a Windows runner rewrites the working tree, and
# test_all.sh does not survive it: a shebang line ending in a carriage return
# is not a shebang. An `// Output:` comment does survive, because go/ast strips
# a trailing carriage return before an example is compared.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A skill tree is hashed, so git does not get to decide its bytes. Normalizing
# one silently changes a digest, and a fixture that wants a carriage return
# should keep it. Nothing in them has one today.
**/skills/** -text
**/testdata/** -text
